{
  "audio_file": "demo_files/Q1E3aFinal_compressed.m4a",
  "audio_size_bytes": 10565214,
  "elapsed_ms": 60556,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 7.21999979019165,
      "end": 9.600000381469727,
      "text": " When you start a new software project,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.800000190734863,
      "end": 12.699999809265137,
      "text": " you're super excited about the potential of"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.699999809265137,
      "end": 16.219999313354492,
      "text": " the project and you want to get moving as soon as possible,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.0,
      "end": 20.059999465942383,
      "text": " which is great. Often when that project"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.3799991607666,
      "end": 23.8799991607666,
      "text": " matures and you get more customers and you get more users,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.559999465942383,
      "end": 26.239999771118164,
      "text": " things need to change because you start"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.239999771118164,
      "end": 29.139999389648438,
      "text": " getting feedback from your customers. That's one thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.139999389648438,
      "end": 33.099998474121094,
      "text": " The other thing that happens is technologies change."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.65999984741211,
      "end": 34.7400016784668,
      "text": " Database systems might change."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.97999954223633,
      "end": 36.91999816894531,
      "text": " You might have to add a new user interface."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.31999969482422,
      "end": 40.959999084472656,
      "text": " You want to be able to do these things without"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.15999984741211,
      "end": 44.119998931884766,
      "text": " having to rewrite all of the logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.0,
      "end": 46.0,
      "text": " How do you do this?"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.720001220703125,
      "end": 50.70000076293945,
      "text": " I've been running software companies for the past 30 years."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.0,
      "end": 55.29999923706055,
      "text": " At some point, I was, what's the word,"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.58000183105469,
      "end": 58.380001068115234,
      "text": " dismayed or surprised to see how difficult it"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.380001068115234,
      "end": 62.97999954223633,
      "text": " becomes to change things if the logic is all over the place."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.7599983215332,
      "end": 66.5,
      "text": " If you have business logic in your database layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.87999725341797,
      "end": 68.27999877929688,
      "text": " in your business logic layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.45999908447266,
      "end": 70.44000244140625,
      "text": " sometimes in your user interface layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.87999725341797,
      "end": 73.4800033569336,
      "text": " little rules that you've got everywhere,"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.41999816894531,
      "end": 76.26000213623047,
      "text": " then at some point,"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.37999725341797,
      "end": 78.73999786376953,
      "text": " nobody knows really what all these rules are."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.08000183105469,
      "end": 80.13999938964844,
      "text": " This is what happens."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.68000030517578,
      "end": 82.62000274658203,
      "text": " As you're moving really quickly in the beginning,"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.80000305175781,
      "end": 85.37999725341797,
      "text": " somebody asks for a feature and one of"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.37999725341797,
      "end": 87.54000091552734,
      "text": " the developers goes and just adds it somewhere."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.54000091552734,
      "end": 91.33999633789062,
      "text": " If there's no real clear rule where that should be,"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.77999877929688,
      "end": 93.81999969482422,
      "text": " that could be in the front end,"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.0,
      "end": 97.16000366210938,
      "text": " it should be in some form of business logic layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.19999694824219,
      "end": 98.12000274658203,
      "text": " it could be in the database,"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.36000061035156,
      "end": 100.19999694824219,
      "text": " it could be a stored procedure or a view"
    },
    {
      "start": 100.19999694824219,
      "end": 102.16000366210938,
      "text": " or something that contains that logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.80000305175781,
      "end": 107.73999786376953,
      "text": " If this keeps on happening over a few years for a very successful project,"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.0,
      "end": 112.0199966430664,
      "text": " you are stuck because you won't have the time to go"
    },
    {
      "start": 112.0199966430664,
      "end": 114.26000213623047,
      "text": " back and understand what exactly"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.26000213623047,
      "end": 117.16000366210938,
      "text": " are all these little rules that was implemented."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.16000366210938,
      "end": 122.0199966430664,
      "text": " Some of them are micro rules that affect big things"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.0199966430664,
      "end": 126.31999969482422,
      "text": " like the way interest is calculated or the way finances are created."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.12000274658203,
      "end": 131.0800018310547,
      "text": " That's the problem that layers solve."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.74000549316406,
      "end": 134.77999877929688,
      "text": " Layered architecture, specifically what"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.77999877929688,
      "end": 136.55999755859375,
      "text": " we're going to talk about now is clean architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.9199981689453,
      "end": 139.33999633789062,
      "text": " This is the problem that it solves and I'm going to"
    },
    {
      "start": 139.33999633789062,
      "end": 141.47999572753906,
      "text": " talk about this right now really quickly."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.36000061035156,
      "end": 150.16000366210938,
      "text": " In Episode 3, the mission here that we need to do is we"
    },
    {
      "start": 150.16000366210938,
      "end": 154.5,
      "text": " need to refactor our code into these different layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.3000030517578,
      "end": 157.77999877929688,
      "text": " We need to implement a rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.0399932861328,
      "end": 160.17999267578125,
      "text": " that's the dependency rule in clean architecture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.39999389648438,
      "end": 163.25999450683594,
      "text": " that mean that all dependencies point inwards."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.47999572753906,
      "end": 165.16000366210938,
      "text": " Let's talk about this."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.67999267578125,
      "end": 168.44000244140625,
      "text": " So you need to go to Episode 2,"
    },
    {
      "start": 168.52000427246094,
      "end": 170.4199981689453,
      "text": " clone this code, this is the code you'll use."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.4199981689453,
      "end": 172.8800048828125,
      "text": " Look at ReadQuest 3,"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.0,
      "end": 174.72000122070312,
      "text": " this is the instruction for Quest 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.44000244140625,
      "end": 176.17999267578125,
      "text": " Read through all of this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 176.39999389648438,
      "end": 178.75999450683594,
      "text": " read the blog there by Robert C. Martin."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.3000030517578,
      "end": 180.74000549316406,
      "text": " The blog's a bit dated,"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.86000061035156,
      "end": 182.60000610351562,
      "text": " some of the terminology is a bit old."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.8800048828125,
      "end": 185.6999969482422,
      "text": " So I'm going to talk through some of these concepts right now."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.47999572753906,
      "end": 189.89999389648438,
      "text": " Then we need to refactor to the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 190.16000366210938,
      "end": 191.72000122070312,
      "text": " You'll see the different layers over here."
    },
    {
      "start": 192.4199981689453,
      "end": 193.25999450683594,
      "text": " Just go back."
    },
    {
      "start": 193.67999267578125,
      "end": 195.05999755859375,
      "text": " So the application layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 195.4199981689453,
      "end": 197.36000061035156,
      "text": " the domain layer, and the infrastructure layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 197.36000061035156,
      "end": 200.52000427246094,
      "text": " At this point, we're going to implement these four layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 203.47999572753906,
      "end": 205.8800048828125,
      "text": " Sometimes the layers are called something different."
    },
    {
      "start": 206.02000427246094,
      "end": 209.02000427246094,
      "text": " Some people call it presentation layer instead of delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 209.6199951171875,
      "end": 210.66000366210938,
      "text": " Some have more layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 211.25999450683594,
      "end": 214.0800018310547,
      "text": " This will be a great overview of how this works."
    },
    {
      "start": 214.1199951171875,
      "end": 215.5800018310547,
      "text": " So let's keep it simple like this."
    },
    {
      "start": 215.6199951171875,
      "end": 217.5,
      "text": " I love these wording,"
    },
    {
      "start": 217.60000610351562,
      "end": 219.6999969482422,
      "text": " specifically delivery layer because that's where"
    },
    {
      "start": 219.6999969482422,
      "end": 222.10000610351562,
      "text": " your application is delivered to the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 222.16000366210938,
      "end": 225.0,
      "text": " It's also responsible for delivering"
    },
    {
      "start": 225.0,
      "end": 228.10000610351562,
      "text": " incoming messages to the application itself."
    },
    {
      "start": 229.36000061035156,
      "end": 231.8000030517578,
      "text": " Then we'll enforce the dependency rule."
    },
    {
      "start": 231.83999633789062,
      "end": 233.22000122070312,
      "text": " This is going to be a big one,"
    },
    {
      "start": 233.32000732421875,
      "end": 236.8000030517578,
      "text": " and there's an interesting code that you need to write to get this done."
    },
    {
      "start": 237.82000732421875,
      "end": 241.10000610351562,
      "text": " That's more of a visual overview of the dependencies."
    },
    {
      "start": 242.5399932861328,
      "end": 245.55999755859375,
      "text": " Then what I also did is I showed you what"
    },
    {
      "start": 245.55999755859375,
      "end": 249.13999938964844,
      "text": " the project structure should look like once you're done."
    },
    {
      "start": 249.77999877929688,
      "end": 252.24000549316406,
      "text": " So this is what you're seeing right here."
    },
    {
      "start": 252.24000549316406,
      "end": 255.02000427246094,
      "text": " Success criteria code is organized into layers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 256.44000244140625,
      "end": 257.5,
      "text": " which is folders."
    },
    {
      "start": 257.8399963378906,
      "end": 260.79998779296875,
      "text": " These are folders described above."
    },
    {
      "start": 261.1000061035156,
      "end": 263.94000244140625,
      "text": " Inner layers do not reference names from the outer layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 264.1000061035156,
      "end": 265.6199951171875,
      "text": " That is the dependency rule."
    },
    {
      "start": 266.0799865722656,
      "end": 269.29998779296875,
      "text": " Any broken dependencies are fixed after the move."
    },
    {
      "start": 270.3399963378906,
      "end": 272.6000061035156,
      "text": " Then just add a docs folder as well."
    },
    {
      "start": 273.260009765625,
      "end": 275.2200012207031,
      "text": " That's just a typical standard."
    },
    {
      "start": 276.0799865722656,
      "end": 278.260009765625,
      "text": " So I'm going to talk you through this."
    },
    {
      "start": 278.3599853515625,
      "end": 279.32000732421875,
      "text": " What is this all about?"
    },
    {
      "start": 279.4599914550781,
      "end": 281.55999755859375,
      "text": " Keep the most important logic separate."
    },
    {
      "start": 281.55999755859375,
      "end": 284.0199890136719,
      "text": " I talked earlier about business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 284.17999267578125,
      "end": 287.32000732421875,
      "text": " We want to keep that into the domain and application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 287.8599853515625,
      "end": 291.1000061035156,
      "text": " Those are the two layers that need to know about business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 291.9800109863281,
      "end": 296.3399963378906,
      "text": " The other layers have infrastructure as well as the delivery mechanisms,"
    },
    {
      "start": 296.4800109863281,
      "end": 299.260009765625,
      "text": " like the fast API or command line interface."
    },
    {
      "start": 299.7200012207031,
      "end": 301.1199951171875,
      "text": " We'll talk about that now."
    },
    {
      "start": 304.4200134277344,
      "end": 306.70001220703125,
      "text": " Problem, when everything is slightly connected,"
    },
    {
      "start": 306.8800048828125,
      "end": 307.79998779296875,
      "text": " changes get harder."
    },
    {
      "start": 308.239990234375,
      "end": 309.5400085449219,
      "text": " That's what I talked about earlier."
    },
    {
      "start": 310.1400146484375,
      "end": 311.8399963378906,
      "text": " Bugs spread farther."
    },
    {
      "start": 312.2799987792969,
      "end": 316.8800048828125,
      "text": " So things are connected all over the place and one thing affects another thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 317.20001220703125,
      "end": 320.94000244140625,
      "text": " And when one thing breaks, everything breaks."
    },
    {
      "start": 322.260009765625,
      "end": 324.7799987792969,
      "text": " That's the bugs spread farther concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 325.20001220703125,
      "end": 328.67999267578125,
      "text": " Testing becomes painful because now you need to test everything."
    },
    {
      "start": 328.8800048828125,
      "end": 331.94000244140625,
      "text": " You need to test your database, your front end, your business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 332.0199890136719,
      "end": 333.5199890136719,
      "text": " All of this are intertwined."
    },
    {
      "start": 333.739990234375,
      "end": 337.82000732421875,
      "text": " In a clean architecture, you can test only your domain and application."
    },
    {
      "start": 337.82000732421875,
      "end": 341.94000244140625,
      "text": " You can test only your domain logic and then you can also test your application,"
    },
    {
      "start": 343.0799865722656,
      "end": 344.29998779296875,
      "text": " use cases and services."
    },
    {
      "start": 344.82000732421875,
      "end": 347.3599853515625,
      "text": " And then you can go and test infrastructure as well."
    },
    {
      "start": 347.3800048828125,
      "end": 351.4800109863281,
      "text": " But those are the hearts of it and you can keep those tests separate,"
    },
    {
      "start": 352.0400085449219,
      "end": 357.3399963378906,
      "text": " which ends up surprisingly making the test sometimes hundreds of times faster to do."
    },
    {
      "start": 357.4800109863281,
      "end": 360.94000244140625,
      "text": " You can run hundreds of tests within less than a second,"
    },
    {
      "start": 361.0400085449219,
      "end": 366.55999755859375,
      "text": " versus if you need to involve databases, it becomes substantially slower."
    },
    {
      "start": 367.82000732421875,
      "end": 371.55999755859375,
      "text": " So we can do these tests in memory and we're going to talk about that"
    },
    {
      "start": 371.55999755859375,
      "end": 373.3599853515625,
      "text": " when we look at the repository pattern."
    },
    {
      "start": 374.9800109863281,
      "end": 380.0400085449219,
      "text": " And the unit of work, so testing becomes painful, new features becomes riskier"
    },
    {
      "start": 380.0400085449219,
      "end": 384.0400085449219,
      "text": " because now you're changing stuff and it can break stuff in unexpected ways."
    },
    {
      "start": 384.5400085449219,
      "end": 386.29998779296875,
      "text": " Mental models become more complex."
    },
    {
      "start": 386.4200134277344,
      "end": 389.1199951171875,
      "text": " This is the thing that I really have found."
    },
    {
      "start": 389.239990234375,
      "end": 391.9800109863281,
      "text": " If you have a clean architecture, you have this folder structure"
    },
    {
      "start": 392.4800109863281,
      "end": 396.0400085449219,
      "text": " and you have the concept of dependencies only pointing inwards,"
    },
    {
      "start": 396.0400085449219,
      "end": 399.3399963378906,
      "text": " then you have a clear understanding of how everything works,"
    },
    {
      "start": 400.0199890136719,
      "end": 401.70001220703125,
      "text": " which is really important."
    },
    {
      "start": 402.20001220703125,
      "end": 405.5400085449219,
      "text": " Computers don't struggle with this, but software developers do."
    },
    {
      "start": 406.0199890136719,
      "end": 410.32000732421875,
      "text": " And I feel especially now in the world of AI where code can get generated"
    },
    {
      "start": 410.760009765625,
      "end": 413.9200134277344,
      "text": " in its millions of lines in minutes,"
    },
    {
      "start": 414.6199951171875,
      "end": 418.55999755859375,
      "text": " it's really important to keep the structure well organized,"
    },
    {
      "start": 418.94000244140625,
      "end": 421.8599853515625,
      "text": " keep the dependencies well understood,"
    },
    {
      "start": 422.6600036621094,
      "end": 426.20001220703125,
      "text": " have a mental model which you can participate on"
    },
    {
      "start": 426.20001220703125,
      "end": 430.2200012207031,
      "text": " instead of just being an observer and trying to figure out what AI is doing."
    },
    {
      "start": 430.5199890136719,
      "end": 433.1400146484375,
      "text": " That will be a recipe for a disaster."
    },
    {
      "start": 434.0400085449219,
      "end": 437.05999755859375,
      "text": " So I feel it's even more important now to have this."
    },
    {
      "start": 437.3599853515625,
      "end": 440.760009765625,
      "text": " Business rules end up locked to specific tools."
    },
    {
      "start": 441.0199890136719,
      "end": 442.739990234375,
      "text": " That's part of the..."
    },
    {
      "start": 442.739990234375,
      "end": 445.55999755859375,
      "text": " You, for example, have business logic in fast API."
    },
    {
      "start": 445.8999938964844,
      "end": 448.6400146484375,
      "text": " It's a disaster because then if you have a command line interface,"
    },
    {
      "start": 448.760009765625,
      "end": 449.9599914550781,
      "text": " you need to repeat it there."
    },
    {
      "start": 449.9599914550781,
      "end": 452.5799865722656,
      "text": " If you have events coming in, you need to repeat it"
    },
    {
      "start": 452.5799865722656,
      "end": 455.29998779296875,
      "text": " and you end up repeating yourself all the time."
    },
    {
      "start": 456.1000061035156,
      "end": 458.94000244140625,
      "text": " The simple solution, put core business rules in the center,"
    },
    {
      "start": 459.2200012207031,
      "end": 461.32000732421875,
      "text": " put changing technology on the outside,"
    },
    {
      "start": 461.70001220703125,
      "end": 464.05999755859375,
      "text": " fast API is an example, or a command line interface,"
    },
    {
      "start": 464.6600036621094,
      "end": 467.67999267578125,
      "text": " or databases, or messaging infrastructure,"
    },
    {
      "start": 468.1600036621094,
      "end": 469.6600036621094,
      "text": " or authenticating systems."
    },
    {
      "start": 470.1600036621094,
      "end": 472.8800048828125,
      "text": " Keep the center stable even if the outside changes."
    },
    {
      "start": 473.1400146484375,
      "end": 475.1600036621094,
      "text": " Do not couple parts together unnecessarily."
    },
    {
      "start": 475.67999267578125,
      "end": 478.2799987792969,
      "text": " This is a visual overview of the layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 478.6400146484375,
      "end": 481.7200012207031,
      "text": " Delivery on the outside, dependencies pointing inwards,"
    },
    {
      "start": 482.3399963378906,
      "end": 485.4599914550781,
      "text": " infrastructure, application, domain is the heart of the system."
    },
    {
      "start": 486.2200012207031,
      "end": 491.1600036621094,
      "text": " The application layer is like an API that works with the domain."
    },
    {
      "start": 491.32000732421875,
      "end": 493.17999267578125,
      "text": " So they go hand in hand."
    },
    {
      "start": 497.1000061035156,
      "end": 499.5799865722656,
      "text": " I just put these on here so you can see."
    },
    {
      "start": 499.6400146484375,
      "end": 501.0199890136719,
      "text": " When we're talking about the outer layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 501.17999267578125,
      "end": 503.8599853515625,
      "text": " command line interfaces, web APIs, user interfaces,"
    },
    {
      "start": 503.8599853515625,
      "end": 508.9599914550781,
      "text": " incoming events, GraphQL API script, those are the entry points."
    },
    {
      "start": 509.3599853515625,
      "end": 512.8200073242188,
      "text": " That's where you deliver your application logic to."
    },
    {
      "start": 514.1799926757812,
      "end": 517.0599975585938,
      "text": " Also, anything coming in from a script is an example"
    },
    {
      "start": 517.0599975585938,
      "end": 521.4199829101562,
      "text": " or an event that gets delivered to the inner part of your application"
    },
    {
      "start": 521.4199829101562,
      "end": 522.719970703125,
      "text": " from the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 523.1599731445312,
      "end": 525.719970703125,
      "text": " Again, that's why I like the terminology delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 526.8400268554688,
      "end": 529.5399780273438,
      "text": " Infrastructure layer is where you put any infrastructure"
    },
    {
      "start": 529.5399780273438,
      "end": 531.7999877929688,
      "text": " that your application relies on."
    },
    {
      "start": 531.7999877929688,
      "end": 537.52001953125,
      "text": " For example, database, file storage, messaging, external APIs."
    },
    {
      "start": 537.780029296875,
      "end": 541.2000122070312,
      "text": " You might have a Twilio integration or a payment solution integration."
    },
    {
      "start": 541.5,
      "end": 543.280029296875,
      "text": " That will be in the infrastructure layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 543.5800170898438,
      "end": 544.260009765625,
      "text": " Logging authentication."
    },
    {
      "start": 544.9199829101562,
      "end": 546.3200073242188,
      "text": " Then you have the application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 546.52001953125,
      "end": 548.739990234375,
      "text": " That's where you define your data transfer objects."
    },
    {
      "start": 549.260009765625,
      "end": 551.4400024414062,
      "text": " We're going to talk about that in the next episode."
    },
    {
      "start": 552.6799926757812,
      "end": 557.1799926757812,
      "text": " These could be dictionaries or classes, objects that get sent"
    },
    {
      "start": 557.1799926757812,
      "end": 560.0599975585938,
      "text": " from the delivery layer into the application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 561.1799926757812,
      "end": 565.4400024414062,
      "text": " Application services have use cases and those interact with"
    },
    {
      "start": 565.4400024414062,
      "end": 568.52001953125,
      "text": " and use the domain layer and also interact with the infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "start": 569.1199951171875,
      "end": 573.219970703125,
      "text": " Then you have the heart of the system, the pure rules."
    },
    {
      "start": 573.719970703125,
      "end": 575.4600219726562,
      "text": " These are, this is the domain layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 576.4000244140625,
      "end": 583.0,
      "text": " So, what, back in the day, 20 years ago,"
    },
    {
      "start": 583.9199829101562,
      "end": 587.3200073242188,
      "text": " before that, code was just all in a bunch of files."
    },
    {
      "start": 587.3200073242188,
      "end": 590.719970703125,
      "text": " Similar to episode two, when we wrapped up episode two,"
    },
    {
      "start": 590.9400024414062,
      "end": 593.8200073242188,
      "text": " you had all of your code files in one big folder there."
    },
    {
      "start": 594.5399780273438,
      "end": 596.239990234375,
      "text": " That's the way it used to be."
    },
    {
      "start": 597.0800170898438,
      "end": 601.260009765625,
      "text": " But at least we separated them into some logical files."
    },
    {
      "start": 603.1599731445312,
      "end": 605.6400146484375,
      "text": " Steps back and it would be one big file of code."
    },
    {
      "start": 606.719970703125,
      "end": 610.9600219726562,
      "text": " So, then people introduced a three-layered architecture"
    },
    {
      "start": 610.9600219726562,
      "end": 613.0800170898438,
      "text": " or sometimes four-layered architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 613.5999755859375,
      "end": 616.780029296875,
      "text": " That would be you're keeping your logic separate."
    },
    {
      "start": 616.780029296875,
      "end": 620.239990234375,
      "text": " You have your presentation layer and then you have a business logic layer"
    },
    {
      "start": 620.239990234375,
      "end": 622.219970703125,
      "text": " and then you have the data access layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 623.4199829101562,
      "end": 625.8800048828125,
      "text": " Notice that the bottom layer here is the database"
    },
    {
      "start": 625.8800048828125,
      "end": 628.3200073242188,
      "text": " and everything depends on the database,"
    },
    {
      "start": 628.9400024414062,
      "end": 631.9600219726562,
      "text": " which is the exact opposite of what I just showed you."
    },
    {
      "start": 632.5800170898438,
      "end": 636.7000122070312,
      "text": " I want to compare clean architecture now to three-layered architecture"
    },
    {
      "start": 638.5999755859375,
      "end": 640.6400146484375,
      "text": " or three-tiered architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 641.219970703125,
      "end": 646.0800170898438,
      "text": " Clean architecture, you are, your primary goal is decoupling logic"
    },
    {
      "start": 646.0800170898438,
      "end": 647.02001953125,
      "text": " from technology."
    },
    {
      "start": 648.219970703125,
      "end": 650.8200073242188,
      "text": " Now, in three-tiered architecture, that's not the goal"
    },
    {
      "start": 650.8200073242188,
      "end": 653.1799926757812,
      "text": " because everything is coupled to the database."
    },
    {
      "start": 653.9400024414062,
      "end": 659.8200073242188,
      "text": " So, you're basically separating the tiers into logical responsibilities"
    },
    {
      "start": 659.8200073242188,
      "end": 661.3800048828125,
      "text": " or functional responsibilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 662.02001953125,
      "end": 665.8800048828125,
      "text": " The center of the architecture in clean architecture is the domain."
    },
    {
      "start": 666.3400268554688,
      "end": 668.280029296875,
      "text": " That's the heart of the business rules."
    },
    {
      "start": 668.8800048828125,
      "end": 672.4600219726562,
      "text": " And this was, what was his name?"
    },
    {
      "start": 673.0599975585938,
      "end": 675.760009765625,
      "text": " So, Robert C. Martin expanded on this in his book,"
    },
    {
      "start": 675.760009765625,
      "end": 681.260009765625,
      "text": " Clean Architecture, but the original book was Domain Driven Design."
    },
    {
      "start": 682.3599853515625,
      "end": 688.1199951171875,
      "text": " Domain Driven Design clarified this idea that if you keep your domain simple,"
    },
    {
      "start": 688.5399780273438,
      "end": 692.2999877929688,
      "text": " it becomes easy to understand what the application does."
    },
    {
      "start": 692.6599731445312,
      "end": 694.97998046875,
      "text": " Everything else becomes a technical concern."
    },
    {
      "start": 695.52001953125,
      "end": 699.1799926757812,
      "text": " But if you want to understand what the business logic is,"
    },
    {
      "start": 699.2000122070312,
      "end": 702.6799926757812,
      "text": " you look at your domain and then you'll go one step further."
    },
    {
      "start": 702.739990234375,
      "end": 704.260009765625,
      "text": " You look at your application layer"
    },
    {
      "start": 704.260009765625,
      "end": 709.1799926757812,
      "text": " and combining those two, you will have all of your business logic right there"
    },
    {
      "start": 709.1799926757812,
      "end": 711.3200073242188,
      "text": " and anything else will sit on the outside."
    },
    {
      "start": 711.9400024414062,
      "end": 715.5599975585938,
      "text": " And it's not messing around with your mental model"
    },
    {
      "start": 715.5599975585938,
      "end": 717.5,
      "text": " of understanding what this should do."
    },
    {
      "start": 718.4199829101562,
      "end": 720.6799926757812,
      "text": " So, whereas with a three-tiered architecture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 720.9000244140625,
      "end": 724.719970703125,
      "text": " you have the database at the center, the schema at the center."
    },
    {
      "start": 725.3800048828125,
      "end": 728.5,
      "text": " Flexibility, clean architecture is highly flexible."
    },
    {
      "start": 728.6799926757812,
      "end": 731.3200073242188,
      "text": " You can swap a SQL database, no SQL."
    },
    {
      "start": 731.3200073242188,
      "end": 734.1400146484375,
      "text": " People always talk about swapping."
    },
    {
      "start": 734.8400268554688,
      "end": 737.719970703125,
      "text": " Now, it doesn't happen often that you want to swap the database."
    },
    {
      "start": 738.5399780273438,
      "end": 740.9000244140625,
      "text": " So, I don't like that as an example."
    },
    {
      "start": 742.0,
      "end": 744.280029296875,
      "text": " One of the biggest benefits that you do get"
    },
    {
      "start": 744.280029296875,
      "end": 748.5800170898438,
      "text": " is all these other little technologies like FastAPI can be changed."
    },
    {
      "start": 749.3400268554688,
      "end": 754.280029296875,
      "text": " In a clean architecture, you would be able to take a FastAPI"
    },
    {
      "start": 754.280029296875,
      "end": 757.219970703125,
      "text": " and change that to the next big thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 757.9600219726562,
      "end": 759.9600219726562,
      "text": " Only a few years ago, it was Flask."
    },
    {
      "start": 759.9600219726562,
      "end": 763.280029296875,
      "text": " And you would be able to change Flask to FastAPI"
    },
    {
      "start": 764.2000122070312,
      "end": 766.0999755859375,
      "text": " without changing any other layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 766.97998046875,
      "end": 768.8599853515625,
      "text": " without touching any other layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 769.0800170898438,
      "end": 770.7000122070312,
      "text": " You'll only touch the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 772.52001953125,
      "end": 774.8599853515625,
      "text": " You'll add a new command line interface"
    },
    {
      "start": 774.8800048828125,
      "end": 778.6599731445312,
      "text": " or you will adopt instead of a certain messaging system,"
    },
    {
      "start": 778.9600219726562,
      "end": 782.0,
      "text": " start using gRPC without touching any other layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 782.260009765625,
      "end": 784.739990234375,
      "text": " That's where the flexibility really comes in."
    },
    {
      "start": 784.8599853515625,
      "end": 786.2999877929688,
      "text": " That's the one big advantage."
    },
    {
      "start": 786.739990234375,
      "end": 788.7000122070312,
      "text": " The other thing is the mental model,"
    },
    {
      "start": 788.7000122070312,
      "end": 792.5599975585938,
      "text": " the simplicity to understand what's going on in all of these layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 793.0399780273438,
      "end": 796.47998046875,
      "text": " In a three-tiered architecture, the flexibility is moderate."
    },
    {
      "start": 796.9199829101562,
      "end": 800.0399780273438,
      "text": " Changing the database often requires rewriting parts of the business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 800.2999877929688,
      "end": 802.3400268554688,
      "text": " Again, I don't want to focus on the database here."
    },
    {
      "start": 803.1199951171875,
      "end": 805.7000122070312,
      "text": " I want to show you something, though."
    },
    {
      "start": 805.7000122070312,
      "end": 806.760009765625,
      "text": " If you look at this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 808.239990234375,
      "end": 811.0,
      "text": " the arrows there are not talking about dependencies."
    },
    {
      "start": 812.3400268554688,
      "end": 814.8200073242188,
      "text": " The dependencies in a three-tiered architecture"
    },
    {
      "start": 814.8200073242188,
      "end": 816.7000122070312,
      "text": " often are all over the place."
    },
    {
      "start": 817.4199829101562,
      "end": 819.760009765625,
      "text": " It's not such a big thing to say that,"
    },
    {
      "start": 820.0599975585938,
      "end": 821.5800170898438,
      "text": " oh, you need to..."
    },
    {
      "start": 821.5800170898438,
      "end": 823.6799926757812,
      "text": " nothing needs to depend on something else."
    },
    {
      "start": 824.239990234375,
      "end": 827.1599731445312,
      "text": " And that often becomes very messy,"
    },
    {
      "start": 827.280029296875,
      "end": 830.6400146484375,
      "text": " whereas with clean architecture, you have an unbreakable rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 831.9000244140625,
      "end": 832.780029296875,
      "text": " the dependency rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 833.8200073242188,
      "end": 835.4600219726562,
      "text": " where everything points inwards."
    },
    {
      "start": 835.6799926757812,
      "end": 837.5399780273438,
      "text": " So I'm just bringing this up again."
    },
    {
      "start": 837.6400146484375,
      "end": 841.719970703125,
      "text": " And then for a more clear view of the dependency rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 841.780029296875,
      "end": 842.6799926757812,
      "text": " look at this graph."
    },
    {
      "start": 843.260009765625,
      "end": 847.5399780273438,
      "text": " It's often misunderstood that you have to go through all the layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 847.8200073242188,
      "end": 848.52001953125,
      "text": " It's not the case."
    },
    {
      "start": 849.1599731445312,
      "end": 852.219970703125,
      "text": " The delivery layer can talk directly to any other layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 853.0800170898438,
      "end": 854.8800048828125,
      "text": " The only thing is,"
    },
    {
      "start": 854.9600219726562,
      "end": 856.760009765625,
      "text": " the delivery layer knows about all layers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 856.8599853515625,
      "end": 858.0800170898438,
      "text": " because it's the outside."
    },
    {
      "start": 858.6799926757812,
      "end": 861.5399780273438,
      "text": " But the moment you move one layer into the infrastructure layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 861.6799926757812,
      "end": 864.780029296875,
      "text": " it should not know anything about the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 864.9400024414062,
      "end": 867.5599975585938,
      "text": " So you should not even mention FastAPI there."
    },
    {
      "start": 867.8400268554688,
      "end": 870.9400024414062,
      "text": " This does become challenging from a programming point of view"
    },
    {
      "start": 870.9400024414062,
      "end": 875.97998046875,
      "text": " when you use this concept of programming against interfaces"
    },
    {
      "start": 875.97998046875,
      "end": 877.6599731445312,
      "text": " instead of implementations,"
    },
    {
      "start": 877.9000244140625,
      "end": 881.7999877929688,
      "text": " which we're going to look at in this episode as well,"
    },
    {
      "start": 881.8800048828125,
      "end": 884.8599853515625,
      "text": " because it affects us with the repository."
    },
    {
      "start": 885.280029296875,
      "end": 887.5,
      "text": " If you look at episode two's code,"
    },
    {
      "start": 887.5399780273438,
      "end": 889.8599853515625,
      "text": " you'll see that the repository is mentioned"
    },
    {
      "start": 890.0800170898438,
      "end": 893.2999877929688,
      "text": " and imported into the application layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 893.5599975585938,
      "end": 894.280029296875,
      "text": " which is wrong."
    },
    {
      "start": 894.8400268554688,
      "end": 897.9199829101562,
      "text": " Big challenge for you is going to be how do you solve that?"
    },
    {
      "start": 898.52001953125,
      "end": 902.3800048828125,
      "text": " How do you still keep a structure in the application layer"
    },
    {
      "start": 902.3800048828125,
      "end": 903.8200073242188,
      "text": " without mentioning JSON?"
    },
    {
      "start": 905.8200073242188,
      "end": 908.02001953125,
      "text": " Application layer should not know about JSON."
    },
    {
      "start": 908.6400146484375,
      "end": 913.0999755859375,
      "text": " You should be able to swap JSON to, let's say, Postgres"
    },
    {
      "start": 913.0999755859375,
      "end": 915.0399780273438,
      "text": " without touching the application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 916.4199829101562,
      "end": 920.3599853515625,
      "text": " Or JSON to Firebase without touching the..."
    },
    {
      "start": 920.3599853515625,
      "end": 922.8400268554688,
      "text": " You should even be able to support multiples."
    },
    {
      "start": 923.3800048828125,
      "end": 925.219970703125,
      "text": " And often we see this with testing."
    },
    {
      "start": 925.3599853515625,
      "end": 926.8200073242188,
      "text": " Once you start testing the application,"
    },
    {
      "start": 926.8200073242188,
      "end": 928.8599853515625,
      "text": " you won't test it with JSON."
    },
    {
      "start": 929.1199951171875,
      "end": 932.280029296875,
      "text": " You'll test it with an in-memory memory store"
    },
    {
      "start": 932.3200073242188,
      "end": 936.260009765625,
      "text": " to get that sub-second speed for all of your tests."
    },
    {
      "start": 936.4000244140625,
      "end": 938.5,
      "text": " If you run 100 tests, 200, 300 tests,"
    },
    {
      "start": 938.5399780273438,
      "end": 941.6199951171875,
      "text": " you'll want that to execute in seconds, not minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 942.260009765625,
      "end": 946.8400268554688,
      "text": " And that's going to be part of what we'll see how to do"
    },
    {
      "start": 947.0800170898438,
      "end": 948.5,
      "text": " in this episode."
    },
    {
      "start": 950.9000244140625,
      "end": 953.5399780273438,
      "text": " So the layers, those are the layers I talked about."
    },
    {
      "start": 954.719970703125,
      "end": 955.3200073242188,
      "text": " Domain."
    },
    {
      "start": 957.52001953125,
      "end": 960.3400268554688,
      "text": " I've mentioned the domain, application layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 960.780029296875,
      "end": 962.1400146484375,
      "text": " data transfer objects."
    },
    {
      "start": 963.0399780273438,
      "end": 964.3800048828125,
      "text": " We use Pydantic for that."
    },
    {
      "start": 964.5,
      "end": 966.47998046875,
      "text": " We've already touched on that in episode one and two."
    },
    {
      "start": 967.4600219726562,
      "end": 970.7000122070312,
      "text": " Now, the data transfer objects transfer data"
    },
    {
      "start": 970.7000122070312,
      "end": 972.760009765625,
      "text": " from the delivery layer to the application layer"
    },
    {
      "start": 972.760009765625,
      "end": 974.7000122070312,
      "text": " or other layers in a standard way."
    },
    {
      "start": 974.6400146484375,
      "end": 977.6799926757812,
      "text": " Typically, application layer, where we unpack it"
    },
    {
      "start": 977.6799926757812,
      "end": 980.1400146484375,
      "text": " and we start going through the use cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 983.4600219726562,
      "end": 984.0599975585938,
      "text": " Infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "start": 985.0,
      "end": 987.5800170898438,
      "text": " The main rule, inner parts should not depend on outer parts."
    },
    {
      "start": 987.6799926757812,
      "end": 988.52001953125,
      "text": " We talked about that."
    },
    {
      "start": 989.0800170898438,
      "end": 991.3200073242188,
      "text": " The core should not know about the infrastructure"
    },
    {
      "start": 991.3200073242188,
      "end": 992.7000122070312,
      "text": " or delivery details."
    },
    {
      "start": 993.1599731445312,
      "end": 995.2999877929688,
      "text": " Dependencies should point inwards."
    },
    {
      "start": 999.0999755859375,
      "end": 1000.219970703125,
      "text": " Why this helps?"
    },
    {
      "start": 1001.52001953125,
      "end": 1003.3400268554688,
      "text": " Anything we do has to have a reason."
    },
    {
      "start": 1004.239990234375,
      "end": 1005.6599731445312,
      "text": " Easier to test the core logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 1005.9000244140625,
      "end": 1006.7000122070312,
      "text": " We talked about that."
    },
    {
      "start": 1006.9600219726562,
      "end": 1008.239990234375,
      "text": " Tests become super fast."
    },
    {
      "start": 1008.6199951171875,
      "end": 1010.1199951171875,
      "text": " They also become isolated."
    },
    {
      "start": 1010.1199951171875,
      "end": 1012.47998046875,
      "text": " You can test the domain on its own,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1012.719970703125,
      "end": 1014.7999877929688,
      "text": " then application use cases on its own"
    },
    {
      "start": 1014.7999877929688,
      "end": 1016.6199951171875,
      "text": " without even touching technology."
    },
    {
      "start": 1017.7999877929688,
      "end": 1022.8200073242188,
      "text": " The advantages are simpler tests as well as super fast tests."
    },
    {
      "start": 1024.1199951171875,
      "end": 1025.52001953125,
      "text": " Easier to change tools later."
    },
    {
      "start": 1025.719970703125,
      "end": 1026.5400390625,
      "text": " You can swap out."
    },
    {
      "start": 1026.800048828125,
      "end": 1027.4599609375,
      "text": " We talked about that."
    },
    {
      "start": 1027.760009765625,
      "end": 1029.1800537109375,
      "text": " Easier to understand the system."
    },
    {
      "start": 1029.4599609375,
      "end": 1031.300048828125,
      "text": " Mental model becomes super simple"
    },
    {
      "start": 1031.5400390625,
      "end": 1034.3800048828125,
      "text": " or at least much more simpler"
    },
    {
      "start": 1034.43994140625,
      "end": 1035.8599853515625,
      "text": " than what it would have been"
    },
    {
      "start": 1036.3399658203125,
      "end": 1039.3399658203125,
      "text": " in a big ball of mud where everything talks to everything."
    },
    {
      "start": 1039.3399658203125,
      "end": 1042.219970703125,
      "text": " Less risk when making updates."
    },
    {
      "start": 1042.8399658203125,
      "end": 1043.9599609375,
      "text": " This is a big one."
    },
    {
      "start": 1044.3800048828125,
      "end": 1047.4200439453125,
      "text": " Systems need to remain flexible, ready for change."
    },
    {
      "start": 1048.4000244140625,
      "end": 1051.300048828125,
      "text": " And if everything's depending on everything else,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1051.6800537109375,
      "end": 1053.9000244140625,
      "text": " change becomes risky"
    },
    {
      "start": 1053.97998046875,
      "end": 1058.0799560546875,
      "text": " and due to that high risk is often not done."
    },
    {
      "start": 1058.8399658203125,
      "end": 1060.93994140625,
      "text": " Which means you get stuck in the mud."
    },
    {
      "start": 1061.4599609375,
      "end": 1065.9599609375,
      "text": " I used to travel with 4x4 in Africa."
    },
    {
      "start": 1066.5999755859375,
      "end": 1069.800048828125,
      "text": " I've got amazing photos of where we got stuck in the mud."
    },
    {
      "start": 1070.219970703125,
      "end": 1071.3199462890625,
      "text": " And interestingly enough,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1071.3199462890625,
      "end": 1075.280029296875,
      "text": " they call this system that everything depends on everything"
    },
    {
      "start": 1075.280029296875,
      "end": 1076.3399658203125,
      "text": " a big ball of mud."
    },
    {
      "start": 1076.8599853515625,
      "end": 1078.3399658203125,
      "text": " I would just say,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1078.3599853515625,
      "end": 1079.9599609375,
      "text": " it just reminds me back in the day"
    },
    {
      "start": 1079.9599609375,
      "end": 1082.06005859375,
      "text": " where a vehicle would get stuck in the mud."
    },
    {
      "start": 1082.219970703125,
      "end": 1084.239990234375,
      "text": " And sometimes I have stories"
    },
    {
      "start": 1084.8199462890625,
      "end": 1087.1400146484375,
      "text": " where we were stuck for two days in the mud"
    },
    {
      "start": 1087.5799560546875,
      "end": 1088.9000244140625,
      "text": " in a Land Cruiser."
    },
    {
      "start": 1089.4599609375,
      "end": 1091.260009765625,
      "text": " So that's what you don't want."
    },
    {
      "start": 1091.3199462890625,
      "end": 1092.5,
      "text": " You want to stay nimble."
    },
    {
      "start": 1092.56005859375,
      "end": 1094.1600341796875,
      "text": " You want to have a Lamborghini"
    },
    {
      "start": 1094.1600341796875,
      "end": 1095.8800048828125,
      "text": " or a Corvette"
    },
    {
      "start": 1096.0799560546875,
      "end": 1099.93994140625,
      "text": " or name your car, Porsche."
    },
    {
      "start": 1100.219970703125,
      "end": 1102.219970703125,
      "text": " And you want to be able to always move,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1102.6199951171875,
      "end": 1103.9000244140625,
      "text": " move your application forward,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1104.43994140625,
      "end": 1107.3599853515625,
      "text": " adapt to business needs without getting stuck."
    },
    {
      "start": 1108.3599853515625,
      "end": 1109.780029296875,
      "text": " Biggest, biggest benefit."
    },
    {
      "start": 1111.260009765625,
      "end": 1111.8199462890625,
      "text": " Key takeaways."
    },
    {
      "start": 1112.260009765625,
      "end": 1114.280029296875,
      "text": " Protect business logic from changing technology."
    },
    {
      "start": 1115.93994140625,
      "end": 1117.6600341796875,
      "text": " Keep the important rules at the center."
    },
    {
      "start": 1119.0999755859375,
      "end": 1122.9599609375,
      "text": " Build so the core stays clean and stable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1124.6600341796875,
      "end": 1128.239990234375,
      "text": " I would say mental model needs to be added here."
    },
    {
      "start": 1129.239990234375,
      "end": 1130.8399658203125,
      "text": " Keep the mental model simple."
    },
    {
      "start": 1131.6800537109375,
      "end": 1134.699951171875,
      "text": " So somebody asked one of the great developers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1136.1400146484375,
      "end": 1137.93994140625,
      "text": " I can't really remember who he was,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1138.0,
      "end": 1140.300048828125,
      "text": " but he's quoted in this book, Clean Architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 1140.6600341796875,
      "end": 1142.800048828125,
      "text": " What is a clean architecture?"
    },
    {
      "start": 1143.02001953125,
      "end": 1145.8599853515625,
      "text": " And he said it's code that can fit into your head."
    },
    {
      "start": 1146.43994140625,
      "end": 1149.260009765625,
      "text": " And what it means is it's code that's easy to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 1150.3399658203125,
      "end": 1152.93994140625,
      "text": " And obviously that doesn't have anything to do with a computer."
    },
    {
      "start": 1152.93994140625,
      "end": 1155.02001953125,
      "text": " The machine, the PC, the Mac."
    },
    {
      "start": 1155.6400146484375,
      "end": 1157.0799560546875,
      "text": " It doesn't need to understand the code."
    },
    {
      "start": 1157.3399658203125,
      "end": 1157.97998046875,
      "text": " It runs the code."
    },
    {
      "start": 1158.760009765625,
      "end": 1160.260009765625,
      "text": " This is for us to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 1160.52001953125,
      "end": 1162.780029296875,
      "text": " It's for us to stay involved, stay in control,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1162.780029296875,
      "end": 1166.280029296875,
      "text": " and easily be able to change things and keep things stable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1168.739990234375,
      "end": 1170.6199951171875,
      "text": " And that's sort of the story."
    },
    {
      "start": 1171.8199462890625,
      "end": 1175.93994140625,
      "text": " Go ahead, implement Quest 1, Episode 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 1176.0999755859375,
      "end": 1180.300048828125,
      "text": " I will see you in the code through of this quest."
    },
    {
      "start": 1180.300048828125,
      "end": 1183.199951171875,
      "text": " By the way, I'm going to use Codex to code through it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1183.9200439453125,
      "end": 1185.300048828125,
      "text": " I've already done it, actually."
    },
    {
      "start": 1185.5400390625,
      "end": 1186.300048828125,
      "text": " It was mind-blowing."
    },
    {
      "start": 1186.699951171875,
      "end": 1190.6199951171875,
      "text": " I'm excited for you to see how I use Codex to implement this quest."
    },
    {
      "start": 1190.699951171875,
      "end": 1193.260009765625,
      "text": " And I've got some interesting takeaways on that."
    },
    {
      "start": 1193.6800537109375,
      "end": 1194.5400390625,
      "text": " See you in the next episode."
    },
    {
      "start": 1194.9200439453125,
      "end": 1195.02001953125,
      "text": " Cheers."
    }
  ],
